      "lineNbr": 244,
      "author": {
        "id": 1123814
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-09-22T20:11:44Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "ANASUBMODE is always set in this function independent of Rp or Rd pull type. It\u0027s at the beginning of this function.\n\n\t/*\n\t * Always set ANASUBMODE to match desired Rp. TCPM layer has a valid\n\t * range of 0, 1, or 2. This range maps to 1, 2, or 3 in ucpd for\n\t * ANASUBMODE.\n\t */\n\tcr \u0026\u003d ~STM32_UCPD_CR_ANASUBMODE_MASK;\n\tcr |\u003d STM32_UCPD_CR_ANASUBMODE_VAL(UCPD_RP_TO_ANASUB(rp));",
      "parentUuid": "c1be9493_830f1aa6",
      "revId": "e94a4078ccf5f457d3e41f8126e27a6bf3d6de87",
