      "writtenOn": "2020-09-22T20:11:44Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I added a comment noting where this info can be found in both the usb-pd spec and the stm32g4 RM0440 document.\n\nThe RXORDSETR is used to determine which type of usb-pd messages will be detected by the ucpd block. But for tx, the ordered set needs to be written before each tx packet (or assumed to be correct from the last time a message was sent). These values aren\u0027t used in this CL as it\u0027s only adding type-c support (as a way to add logical pieces of the driver).",
      "parentUuid": "50f62e25_db2cd5ed",
